This repository is published so people can use the HIC! website and download the
desktop app for personal use. No licence is granted to copy, modify, redistribute,
republish or create derivative works from the code, design or written content
(translations, scene notes and texts) in this repository, in whole or in part,
without written permission from the copyright holder.

The Bayeux Tapestry itself (11th century) is in the public domain. The tapestry
photographs in tapestry/ come from the 2017 high-resolution photography by the
Université de Caen Normandie with the Bayeux Museum, published on Wikimedia Commons
(files "Tapisserie de Bayeux, p1.jpg" and "p2.jpg") and marked public domain there as
faithful reproductions of a two-dimensional public-domain work. Their reuse is
governed by that status, not by this licence. The Latin inscriptions are the
tapestry's own.

Medieval captions are written by Claude via each user's own Anthropic API key.
Use of Claude is subject to Anthropic's own terms.
